.SH "Motivation"
.PP
To be able to write PDE equations in finite element form, using the CSMP Algorithm class\&.

.PP
RULES for using righthand Mathoperators

.PP
.IP "1." 4
supplied data:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Property vectors contain data from: nodes, integration points, or elements
.IP "  \(bu" 4
node and integration point data are supplied together in a numbering as specified for the particular element type\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
if a node or a integration point has multiple degrees of freedom, then the node property \fBvector<double>\fP will be of dimension (nds+ips) * dof in this case, the entries will be 'dof' per node or constraint point in the order as given above\&. 
.PP

.PP

